[Music]  six years after its release skyrim still  manages to be relevant between the 2016  remaster the upcoming VR version and now  a switch port it's hard to forget about  the Elder Scrolls 5 and that's a  testament to how absorbing an RPG it is  with the addition of instant portability  on switch and the high quality of the  port itself it's now even harder to put  down Skyrim is one of the best switch  ports currently available though it's  not too surprising considering the  game's age it runs smoothly with a  rock-solid framerate in both smaller  spaces and in the overworld text can be  a little small when playing handheld  though it still plays as well as it does  docked him with a pro controller motion  controls are all optional as well  wagging a joy Conn will swing a sword  and moving your controller of choice  will aim your bow Skyrim does retain the  expected glitches fans have come to love  though including Bazaar and PC pathing  problems in our 10 hours testing the  game we didn't find any new bugs so it's  just the silly charming weirdness you  might remember in Whiterun the main  edition on switch is amiibo  compatibility which is there only if you  really want to try it  amiibo uses nested in the magic menu  under powers and you have to cast it the  way you would any other power before  tapping an ebow to the NFC reader like  in breath of the wild using amiibo isn't  a guarantee of good loot in this case  Zelda amiibo give you a chance to get  links spread the wild tunic the Master  Sword and the Hylian Shield that you  might get a chest filled with arrows or  an assortment of meats instead you can  use each amiibo once per day but we were  able to get all the cool gear in one day  using a few Zelda amiibo around the  office as a bonus the gear actually was  better than any of the early game armor  and weapons all other amiibo will get  you a basic loot chest the quality of  the port decides Skyrim has certainly  aged since it first released in 2011 the  off maligned sword and shield combat has  fared the most poorly of course since it  never felt great two columns leaving the  sword around in the first place there's  also no mod support currently so if  you're used to quality of life mods it  can be weird to go back to regular old  Skyrim even if you still find its quirks  charming  but the original version of Skyrim is  still an immense engrossing RPG and the  quality number and variety of its quests  makes it easy to become as lost in its  world as ever  there's so much to do in Skyrim that  it's likely you haven't done it all yet  and because it's now portable you can  pick up and play for shorter verse that  can easily turn into hours with the  addition of Zelda themed gear that's  actually useful and the fact that you  can play anywhere the switch version of  Skyrim is a great opportunity to revisit  a much-loved RPG for more on Skyrim you  can check out our impressions of the  special edition and our original review  on GameSpot  [Music]

